-per-100 mj-outlook-group-fix\" style=\"font-size:0px;text-align:left;direction:ltr;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:100%;\">\n        \n      <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"vertical-align:top;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;\">\n              \n    <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"\" width=\"100%\">\n          <tbody>\n            \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <p style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:100%;\">\n      </p>\n      \n      <!--[if mso | IE]><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:520px;\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"520px\" ><tr><td style=\"height:0;line-height:0;\"> &nbsp;\n</td></tr></table><![endif]-->\n    \n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><h2 style=\"margin-top: 14pt;margin-bottom: 4pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Make This Your Last Miserable Tax Season Ever</span></h2><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Sara,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">It\u2019s the day before the deadline and in the last few weeks I\u2019ve been getting A LOT of emails and calls from former clients saying \u2018I\u2019m never doing this again, find me a buyer or I\u2019m burning it down\u2019</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If the thought of one more tax season makes you want to lock the door and throw your laptop in the ocean\u2026 you\u2019re not alone.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Here\u2019s the good news: You\u2019ve got options. Whether you want to offload your firm completely or just lighten your load, now\u2019s the time to act\u2014not mid-February when you\u2019re buried in 1099s and caffeine. I know you\u2019re tired and you simply cannot add on, but save this email for next week because May is the perfect time to make sure you do not do this to yourself yet again.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Here\u2019s your \u201cget-out-of-misery\u201d menu:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>1. Sell Your Firm and Walk Away</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If you\u2019re done-done\u2014burned out, over it, and ready for the next chapter\u2014you can sell 100% of your firm and exit entirely. With the right buyer and a clean transition plan, you\u2019ll likely get paid for what you\u2019ve built and never have to file another extension (except your own from your sailboat)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>2. Sell Your Firm and Stay On (Without the Stress)</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Hand off ownership, keep your favorite clients, and show up like a normal employee\u2014minus the late nights, payroll stress, or management headaches. Many buyers offer rollover equity, letting you cash out partially now and still benefit from future growth or resale.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>3. Sell a Majority, Keep a Minority Stake</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This is the \"have your cake and eat it too\" option. Sell a majority stake to a partner who takes over operations, while you keep a seat at the table (and some future upside). Can be perfect if you still love the work but not the grind of running the firm.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>4. Merge with a Larger Firm (and Sell into It)</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Join forces with a larger, better-resourced firm. You sell your book into theirs, get support with staffing and tech, and possibly take a leadership or client service role post-merger. This often comes with equity or bonus payouts tied to performance.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>5. Sell Internally with SBA-Backed Financing</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Let a trusted employee or junior partner buy you out over time using SBA financing. You\u2019ll phase out at your pace while mentoring the next generation. Bonus: you can structure this to get your full value and a smoother transition for clients.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>6. Package Your Firm for a Search Fund Buyer</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">There\u2019s a growing pool of motivated buyers\u2014often MBAs with investor backing\u2014who are looking to buy and run firms just like yours. You sell, help them get up to speed for a few months, and then hand over the reins while keeping some seller financing or equity in the deal.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If even one of those options sounds like something you need to do, don\u2019t wait until you\u2019re staring down the barrel of another tax season... reply to this email and let\u2019s make a plan.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">To a smooth tax season,<br>Sara Sharp<strong><br></strong>Partner, SK&amp;S Law Group<br>Business Consultant &amp; Founder of Deal Academy</span></p><p><strong><em>P.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, </em></strong><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/09507895405?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); color: rgb(52, 37, 219)\"><strong><em>fill out this form here</em></strong></span></a><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); color: rgb(52, 37, 219)\"><strong><em>.</em></strong></span></p></div>\n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      \n     <!--[if mso | IE]><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" ><tr><td><![endif]-->\n              <table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"float:none;display:inline-table;\">\n                <tbody>\n                  \n      <tr>\n        <td style=\"padding:0px 4px ;vertical-align:middle;\">\n          <table border=\"0\" 